<item>
<title>Telegram macOS</title>
<description>New:&lt;br&gt;• The emoji panel is built from your Mac's emoji font, so new emoji appear after a macOS update without updating Telegram&lt;br&gt;• Some rarely used animations and 3D scenes download after you log in instead of shipping with the app&lt;br&gt;• Redesigned profiles with a new photo layout, interactive gifts, and an updated music player&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Improved:&lt;br&gt;• Photos, avatars, stickers, GIFs and other images are decoded in a separate sandboxed process, so a malicious image can't reach Telegram's memory, and a screen of photos appears about 20% faster&lt;br&gt;• Animated stickers and emoji are drawn in a separate sandboxed process, so a malicious animation can't reach Telegram's memory&lt;br&gt;• Code blocks are highlighted in a separate sandboxed process: a malicious or huge code block can't crash or freeze Telegram&lt;br&gt;• Widgets run, draw and are checked in one sandboxed process; Telegram itself no longer contains a JavaScript engine or an HTML renderer, and a misbehaving widget can't freeze Telegram&lt;br&gt;• Updates download only the version for your Mac's processor: on Apple Silicon about 44 MB instead of about 200 MB&lt;br&gt;• Starting with the next update, Macs with Apple Silicon download only what changed instead of the whole app&lt;br&gt;• Updates are patched by a small separate sandboxed helper that checks every byte against Telegram's signature&lt;br&gt;• Telegram takes 70 MB less disk space&lt;br&gt;• The share extension uses Telegram's own core instead of carrying a second copy&lt;br&gt;• Lower memory use with link previews, dice and emoji effects, and avatars&lt;br&gt;• Wide-color photos keep their full resolution in the photo editor&lt;br&gt;• Pasted and dropped images keep their original quality and format&lt;br&gt;• Detached chat and profile windows use consistent controls and follow theme changes&lt;br&gt;• Contact Edit matches Profile Details, and its cards use the profile backdrop&lt;br&gt;• Plain gift tiles and ribbons use the profile palette&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Fixed:&lt;br&gt;• Updates check their signature before unpacking and must be signed by Telegram&lt;br&gt;• A broken or malicious sticker can no longer freeze Telegram or stop other animations&lt;br&gt;• The raise-hand animation in voice chats showed nothing&lt;br&gt;• Opening a profile with a personal channel no longer freezes the app&lt;br&gt;• Cancelling a tab swipe keeps the current page, and shared media returns when tabs become available again&lt;br&gt;• Forum topics preserve their context when opening media, replying, or forwarding from pinned messages&lt;br&gt;• In-chat search keeps focus when you use the arrow keys or Backspace&lt;br&gt;• The article editor stays editable after its last attachment is removed, preserves pasted table formatting, and keeps spoilers attached to collage items&lt;br&gt;• Large supported WebP stickers render as stickers, and grouped files can carry captions in slow mode&lt;br&gt;• An incoming or active call stays in place when another outgoing request finishes late&lt;br&gt;• StoreKit redelivery no longer reports an older purchase as a new one&lt;br&gt;• Fixed crashes when closing fullscreen videos or navigation windows, reading messages aloud, handling streamed text, editing gift resale prices, during remote logout, story expiration and certain paste operations&lt;br&gt;• Improved stability when opening chats, viewing forum topics, and using widgets&lt;br&gt;• Fixed a playback issue triggered by slow media key and remote control actions&lt;br&gt;• Very large storage sizes display correctly&lt;br&gt;• Story photos keep their location even when other photo metadata can't be read&lt;br&gt;• Profile music titles stay centered when opening a profile or leaving Edit&lt;br&gt;</description>
<pubDate>2026-16-11 08:37:57</pubDate>
